  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new built-in post `FluidNC` (`assets/posts/fluidnc.cps`).\n- A new built-in machine `3040 router (FluidNC)` (`assets/machines/fluidnc-3040.mch`). The machine names `FluidNC` as its post.\n- The registry lists both (`crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`).\n- `FluidNC` is in `M3_ONLY_POSTS` (`crates/app/src/operation/tool_gate.rs`), because the post writes only `M3`. This is the same as `Grbl 1.1`.\n- The posting guide table has a FluidNC row.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/3192-fluidnc-post.md`. Each dialect decision names its FluidNC wiki page.\n\nThe post is `grbl.cps` with these differences:\n- Line 2 of the header is `(FLUIDNC POST - NOT VERIFIED ON A MACHINE)`. This line stays until the owner reports a clean dry run.\n- The refusals and comments name FluidNC.\n- The comments cite the FluidNC wiki pages.\n\nThe words that the post writes are the same as the Grbl 1.1 words:\n- No canned cycles. Drilling is G0 / G1 moves and `G4 P<seconds>`.\n- The tool change is `M5`, a Z lift, a comment, then `M0`. The post writes no `M6` and no `T` word. FluidNC's `M6` acts only through a tool changer or a macro in the YAML file, which the post cannot see.\n- Tapping, boring and `G41`/`G42` are refused by name.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe FluidNC wiki pages could not be fetched in this session (no network permission). The decisions come from FluidNC's documented G-code and M-code lists as the author knows them. The decision file has a table with one row for each point and its wiki page. Please check each row against wiki.fluidnc.com. The owner's AI-made post was not read. No other CAM post or output was read.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (new):\n- `crates/post/tests/script_fluidnc.rs` (binary `script_fluidnc`): the recorded-stream suite (`post_suite!(\"fluidnc.cps\")`) and six FluidNC pins on the 3040:\n  - `fluidnc_header_says_not_verified_on_a_machine`\n  - `fluidnc_tool_change_is_a_stop_without_m6`\n  - `fluidnc_drill_cycle_posts_as_plain_moves_and_a_g4_dwell`\n  - `fluidnc_refuses_spindle_rpm_over_the_3040_maximum`\n  - `fluidnc_refuses_tapping_and_control_compensation_by_name`\n  - `fluidnc_lifts_in_the_work_offset_on_a_machine_with_no_safe_retract`\n- `machine_library::the_linuxcnc_machine_is_offered_the_linuxcnc_post`: the 3040 is offered the FluidNC post.\n- `conformance` (existing, reads the registry): every mill golden posts byte-exact on FluidNC, `tap_plate` is refused by name, and the synth stream is pinned.\n- `machine` (existing): the library list has the 3040 as a mill.\n\nNew top-level test file: `crates/post/tests/script_fluidnc.rs`. Reason: `recorded_streams::every_shipped_post_script_has_its_suite` requires one `script_<stem>.rs` for each shipped post.\n\nRed before the fix: on unchanged code all 17 tests of `script_fluidnc` fail (`assets/posts/fluidnc.cps: No such file or directory`).\n\nMutations (each red, then green after restore):\n- Remove the \"not verified\" header line: `fluidnc_header_says_not_verified_on_a_machine` is red.\n- Write `T<n> M6` in place of the `M0` stop: `fluidnc_tool_change_is_a_stop_without_m6` is red.\n\nGate results on the final tree (head `d031b3ec3`, base upstream/main `e4b08e95b`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: the plan has 859 steps, because the shared goldens reach every app and post suite. The first run passed 702 steps with 0 failed, then stopped at the one-hour limit of the background task. Two re-runs with `--only` covered the rest:\n  - `--only cl --only post`: 147 steps, 0 failed.\n  - `--only app`: 711 steps, 0 failed, 52.9 min.\n  - The `ui lib` step passed in the first run.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. This is a `P6` PR, and AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a heavy step only to a `P1` PR.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNo existing golden moved. New goldens:\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fluidnc/*.nc` (12 files) and `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_fluidnc.nc`.\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/fluidnc/` (11 files).\n\nEach new golden is the same as its `grbl` twin, with two exceptions. The header has the \"not verified\" line. A refusal names `fluidnc.cps` and \"the FluidNC post\".\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No FluidNC machine ran these programs. The header says so.\n- The 3040 values are typical for the class, not a maker's sheet. The owner must confirm them.\n- The FluidNC wiki pages were not read again in this session (see Readings).\n- The `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work` suites ran in the `--only app` run and passed. No catalog program changed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch the same files, but different lines (other rows of the same lists). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`: #4312, #4263, #3982, #2646.\n- `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`: #4288, #4263, #3982, #2646.\n- `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`: #2646.\n\nChangelog: New post \"FluidNC\" and machine \"3040 router (FluidNC)\": the Grbl 1.1 words, drill cycles as plain moves, tool change as M0, the header says the post is not verified on a machine (#3192)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3192\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
